zclassicd developer-tool helpers (zcutil/tools/vendor)

The files under zcutil/tools/vendor/ are copied byte for byte from the Z23 repository
(zclassic23), commit recorded in Z23_SOURCE.tsv, and are licensed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0 (full text in LICENSE.z23):

    Copyright 2026 Rhett Creighton

The rest of zclassicd remains under the MIT license (see COPYING). The copyright holder
of the vendored files and of the developer tools is the same. Individual vendored files
keep whatever notices they carry; those are part of the byte-identical copy.

Vendored files must never be edited in this tree. Provenance and identity checks:
src/c23/tools/check-vendor.sh zcutil/tools/Z23_SOURCE.tsv. A file derived from a Z23 file
with changes is not vendored: it lives outside vendor/ and carries the header
"derived from Z23 <path>@<commit>, changed" (Apache License section 4(b)).

Developer tools only, never linked into zclassicd or the wallet: zcl-dev (glob matcher),
zcl-run (process_group_exec.c, built with -include stdbool.h because the POSIX half of the
upstream file relies on a C23 bool).
